<!--META-DATA
{
	tags: ["struct", "logical_indexing", "for", "while", "isfield", "isa"],
}
-->

<statement>
	<p>
		Given a structure containing car attributes and a filter condition, return a logical indexing vector indicating which entries satisfy the condition.
	</p>
	
	<tabular valign="top" halign="right" top="minor">
		<col width="12%"/>
		<col width="88%" halign="left"/>
			<row>
			<cell>Inputs:</cell>
			<cell>
				<p><pf>data</pf> (1 x 1) struct — from <pf>'carbig.mat'</pf></p>
			</cell>
		</row>
			<row>
				<cell/>
			<cell>
				<p><pf>feature</pf> (1 x N) char vector — the field name (e.g., <pf>'Model'</pf>, <pf>'Weight'</pf>)</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
		<row bottom="minor">
				<cell/>
			<cell>
				<p><pf>value</pf> (1 x 1) double or (1 x M) char vector — the value to match</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
		<row bottom="minor">
			<cell>Outputs:</cell>
			<cell>
				<p><pf>filter</pf> (R x 1) logical vector — column vector of <pf>true</pf>\<pf>false</pf> values.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
			<row>
			<cell>Details:</cell>
			<cell>
				<p>Use <pf>numel</pf>, <pf>size</pf>, or <pf>length</pf> to get the number of values in the list.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
			<row>
				<cell/>
			<cell>
				<p> The k-th value of <pf>index_list</pf> should be <pf>true</pf> if <pf>feature</pf> is a field of <pf>data</pf> AND the k-th value of of this <pf>feature</pf> field is equal to <pf>value</pf>. It should be <pf>false</pf> otherwise.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
			<row>
				<cell/>
			<cell>
				<p>Use a loop to construct the output logical vector.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
			<row>
				<cell/>
			<cell>
				<p>Assume <pf>data</pf> is a non-empty structure vector loaded from <pf>'carbig.mat'</pf>.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
			<row>
				<cell/>
			<cell>
				<p>If <pf>feature</pf> is not a field in <pf>data</pf>, return <pf>[]</pf>.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
			<row>
				<cell/>
			<cell>
				<p>Use <pf>isfield</pf> to test if a char vector names a field; use <pf>isa</pf> to distinguish text vs numbers.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
		<row bottom="minor">
				<cell/>
			<cell>
				<p>You may find <pf>true(m,1)</pf> and <pf>false(m,1)</pf> useful to initialize logical vectors.</p>
			</cell>
		</row>
	</tabular>

	<p>
		Examples:
		<program>
			<code>
				car_data = load('carbig.mat');
				mpg_filter = car_index_filter(car_data, 'MPG', 30);
				% mpg_filter should be a 406x1 logical vector.
				% Use this filter to display all models with an mpg of 30:
				disp(car_data.Model(mpg_filter,:))
				% Expected output shows 7 models with MPG exactly 30.
			</code>
		</program>
	</p>
</statement>
